From: pump
Subject: [PATCH] Bounds-check weight loading: a short weights list throws instead of reading past its end

Every set_weights_ walked the flat weight list with *(it++) on a bare
std::vector<float>::iterator, so a .nam file whose weight count does not
match its architecture read past the end of the list (heap-buffer-overflow
in Conv1D, Conv1x1, LSTMCell, BatchNorm, ... while the network was built).
The cursor is now nam::weights_iterator, which knows the end and throws
std::runtime_error on a read past it. The end-of-load checks use it too
(LSTM's was an assert, so release builds never checked).

---
